      "reasons": [
        "The packet supports that the “conflict interference effect” (e.g., the Stroop effect) is used to study conflict processing and that perceptual conflict is a component, but it does not explicitly define conflict as “interference that arises when different aspects of information or processing are incompatible, making performance more difficult.”",
        "The definition’s wording “making performance more difficult” is not stated in the packet.",
        "The claim that conflict “may include components like perceptual conflict” is directionally supported (perceptual conflict is discussed as a component), but the overall definition relies on unsupported general framing beyond what the packet directly provides."
